From: uDroid graphics runtime
Subject: [PATCH] X11 WSI: make AHB allocation and teardown portable

Make Android headers an explicit build input rather than linking libandroid,
fix portable C++ initialization/includes, and advertise only exportable
AHardwareBuffer surface formats. Preserve the application-selected format from
surface enumeration through image creation, allocation, and DRI3 transport.
Create each swapchain image exactly once so deferred allocation keeps the
application-visible VkImage handle stable. Select memory using the image's real
requirements, preserve sRGB semantics, initialize cleanup state, and wake the
Present event thread during teardown. Bound the private AHardwareBuffer socket
handshake so a dead or mismatched X server cannot freeze the producer. Accept
readable final messages that arrive together with POLLHUP. Private DRI3
modifiers 1257 and 1255 tell the paired Termux:X11 server whether content is
RGBA or BGRA.
---
